cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Crypto3DStackCPU: a cryptographic CPU with a Vertical Trust Fabric for 3D-stacked memory"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "George David"
    family-names: "Tsitlauri"
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics and Telecommunications, University of Thessaly"
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gdtsitlauri/Crypto3DStackCPU"
abstract: >-
  A pipelined cryptographic CPU running encrypted, authenticated programs on a 4-tier 3D-stacked memory
  model. Every inter-tier transfer is authenticated by an AES-CMAC Vertical Trust Fabric with per-epoch,
  per-role keys, anti-replay and a formally verified trust guard. Memory encryption with an integrity tree,
  first-order masking, fault-injection hardening and a PUF-derived root key are implemented in RTL and
  validated in simulation.
keywords: [hardware security, 3D-stacked memory, secure processor, formal verification, fault injection, side channels, PUF, FPGA]
